    "final_output": "I now have everything needed to give you a complete, verified answer.\n\n---\n\n## Wildlife Survey Repository — Source Assessment\n\n### ✅ Approved Current Report\n\n| Field | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| **Report ID** | RPT-2026-017 |\n| **Title** | Wildlife Population Survey Q1 2026 |\n| **Version** | 3.0 |\n| **Status** | **Approved** |\n| **Approved by** | Dr. Sarah Chen |\n| **Approval date** | 2026-04-10 |\n\nThis is the only report in the repository with `status: approved`. The Q4 2025 edition (RPT-2026-009) is **archived**, and the Coastal Bird Survey (RPT-2026-021) is still a **draft** — neither should be used as a policy brief source.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Linked Dataset — WD-2026-001\n\n| Field | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| **Dataset ID** | WD-2026-001 |\n| **Release name** | wolf_population_q1_2026_v3 |\n| **Approved for publication** | **Yes** ✅ |\n| **Current release** | **Yes** ✅ |\n| **Release date** | 2026-04-10 |\n| **Methodology** | GPS collar tracking + aerial survey |\n\nThe dataset is both approved for publication and the current release — no concerns there.\n\n---\n\n### 📌 Key Finding (one sentence)\n\n> Gray wolf populations in the Great Lakes region grew by **8% to 412 individuals** in Q1 2026, based on GPS collar tracking and aerial survey data collected January–March 2026.\n\n---\n\n**Bottom line:** RPT-2026-017 v3.0 is the correct, approved source for the executive policy brief, and its linked dataset (WD-2026-001) is fully cleared — approved for publication and current.",
